  "reveal": {
    "ledger_voiced": "From my book. The sitting ran as I ran it: the guttering of the lamp: a wick trimmed short at six o'clock; it wants ten minutes; the raps: my knee against the table's leaf, twice and thrice; the whispered voice: my own voice, thrown low; grief hears what it is owed; the cold draught: the window cord, loosed an inch before the lamps went out; the table's tilt: the wedge of my boot beneath the claw-foot; the spirit trumpet: black silk thread, and the reach of a practised arm; the scent of violets: a phial in my left sleeve; the right was held.\n\nAs to the evening's business: the account Dr Tobias Quill swore to was an invention, for those hands were out of the dark and about their own work. Captain Wat Frew was past any sitting's reach before the lamps were lit.\n\nThe dead say what it profits me they say; on this occasion they profited Dr Tobias Quill more.",
    "truth": {
      "order": [
        "the guttering of the lamp",
        "the raps",
